<tm:xmi/EAID_789287AA_0B2D_40cf_A249_03E38DB459F6> a tm:Class ;
    rdfs:label "DATED VEHICLE JOURNEY INTERCHANGE" ;
    skos:definition "A VEHICLE JOURNEY INTERCHANGE between two DATED VEHICLE JOURNEYs. It could be created ad-hoc or be based on a planned interchange such as a SERVICE JOURNEY INTERCHANGE, a SERVICE JOURNEY PATTERN INTERCHANGE, or an INTERCHANGE RULE. Notes: An indicator if the interchange should be advertised to the public or not. Notes: The latest time that the distributor vehicle can delay its departure to in the wait for a delayed feeder vehicle. Notes: Identifier of DATED VEHICLE INTERCHANGE. Notes: The shortest time needed for a passenger to traverse the distance from the arrival point of the feeder vehicle to the departure point of the distributor vehicle. Notes: A special marker indicating if the feeder and distributor vehicle journey are run by the same vehicle." ;
    tm:attribute <tm:xmi/EAID_789287AA_0B2D_40cf_A249_03E38DB459F6/attribute/EAID_073152BE_31BD_48c8_8BA3_703CF73510D2>,
