    skos:definition "Characteristics of a process that takes place at a SITE COMPONENT, such as check-in, security screening, ticket control or immigration, that may potentially incur a time penalty that should be allowed for when journey planning. Notes: Access feature associated with CHECK CONSTRAINT. Notes: Direction in which CHECK CONSTRAINT applies: forwards, back or both. For CHECK CONSTRAINT associated with links, corresponds to direction of link. For CHECK CONSTRAINT associated with ENTRANCEs corresponds to direction from outside SITE to inside SITE. Notes: Identifier of CHECK CONSTRAINT. Notes: Name of CHECK CONSTRAINT. Notes: Order of CHECK CONSTRAINT." ;
