    skos:definition "Specialisation of a FLEXIBLE QUAY to identify what is the catchment zone for a hail and ride service (so that a stop finder can find the nearest available types of transport). It is a named zone visited by a particular mode of transport and may be designated by a start point and end point on the road It is part of the Site data set rather than the service data set, since it can be defined and exists indepently of an actual service. Notes: Compass Bearing associated with a HAIL AND RIDE AREA. Notes: Compass Octant associated with a HAIL AND RIDE AREA. Notes: Identifier of a HAIL AND RIDE AREA." ;
