    skos:definition "A CONTROL ACTION consisting in adding a completely new DATED VEHICLE JOURNEY INTERCHANGE between a feeder DATED VEHICLE JOURNEY and a distributor DATED VEHICLE JOURNEY to the latest valid plan. Notes: An indicator if the interchange should be advertised to the public or not. Notes: The latest time that the distributor vehicle can delay its departure to in the wait for passengers from a delayed feeder vehicle. Notes: Identifier of INTERCHANGE CREATION. Notes: The shortest time needed for a passenger to traverse the distance from the arrival point of the feeder vehicle to the departure point of the distributor vehicle. Notes: An indicator if the feeder and distributor vehicle journey are run by the same vehicle." ;
