    skos:definition "Specialisation of LINE for flexible service. As all the service on a LINE may not all be flexible, flexibility itself is described at JOURNEY PATTERN level (meaning that a separate JOURNEY PATTERN is needed for each type of flexibility available for the line). Types of flexible services are : - Virtual line service - Flexible service with main route - Corridor service - Fixed stop area-wide flexible service - Free area-wide flexible service - Mixed types of flexible service - Mixed type of flexible and regular services Notes: Type of FLEXIBLE LINE. Notes: Identifier of FLEXIBLE LINE." ;
