<tm:xmi/EAID_563A8BBC_9CB8_451d_B2F1_CAFB6963C5A2> a tm:Class ;
    rdfs:label "PATH LINK" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <tm:xmi/EAID_053E40C7_BFD2_4dc7_B115_EEF0172609C2>,
        <tm:xmi/EAID_8F917E63_8DDD_460e_AB25_6F1AD3B3E6ED> ;
    skos:definition "A link within a PLACE of or between two PLACEs (that is STOP PLACEs, ACCESS SPACEs or QUAYs,BOARDING POSITIONs,, POINTs OF INTEREST etc or PATH JUNCTIONs) that represents a step in a possible route for pedestrians, cyclists or other out-of-vehicle passengers within or between a PLACE. NOTE: It is possible but not mandatory that a PATH LINK projects onto a more detailed set of infrastructure or mapping links that plot the spatial course, allowing it to be represented on maps and to tracking systems. Notes: Access feature type associated with PATH LINK. Notes: Whether all areas of component are accessible in a Wheelchair. Notes: Allowed direction of use of PATH LINK. Notes: Direction heading to show for PATH LINK when travelling in its TO / FROM sense Notes: Nature of covering of PATH LINK. Notes: Description of PATH LINK. Notes: Whether element is within a gated area. Notes: Identifier of a PATH LINK. Notes: How element is lit. Notes: Maximum number of passengers that can use a PATH LINK. Notes: Number of steps involved in using a PATH LINK. Notes: Type of passage traversed by PATH LINK, if any. This provides a more precis description of Access Feature type. Notes: Number of people that can be in component at a time. Notes: Whether the link is available for PUBLIC use. Notes: Description of a towards direction. Notes: Transition for with PATH LINK: up, down, level." ;
    tm:attribute <tm:xmi/EAID_563A8BBC_9CB8_451d_B2F1_CAFB6963C5A2/attribute/EAID_9A6D635F_0B14_46c7_891B_D5A6A4D573A2>,
        <tm:xmi/EAID_563A8BBC_9CB8_451d_B2F1_CAFB6963C5A2/attribute/EAID_FCC0A534_54A2_41dd_862B_CD18A87652FA>,
