<tm:xmi/EAID_9B14477D_EA87_43df_ABA9_8ED405FC852A> a tm:Class ;
    rdfs:label "SCHEDULED STOP POINT" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <tm:xmi/EAID_971FC364_7043_4d6f_919D_137E30A68145> ;
    skos:definition "A POINT where passengers can board or alight from vehicles. Notes: Whether STOP POINT can be considered as being at the centre of a TOPOGRAPHIC PLACE. Default is false. Notes: Heading of stop relative to street. Degrees from North. This should be considered as a derived value that can be used for presentation purposes when information about the physical stop is not available. . The definitive value is the compass bearing found on the QUAY (ie physical stop) to which a SCHEDULED STOP POINT is assigned. Notes: Description of SCHEDULED STOP POINT. Notes: Default for whether stop may be used for alighting. May be overridden on specific services. Notes: Default for whether stop may be used for boarding . May be overridden on specific services. Notes: Identifier of a SCHEDULED STOP POINT. Notes: Label of SCHEDULED STOP POINT. Notes: Default for whether stop is a request stop. May be overridden in JOURNEY PATTERNs. Notes: Short Name of SCHEDULED STOP POINT. Notes: URL associated with SCHEDULED STOP POINT." ;
    tm:attribute <tm:xmi/EAID_9B14477D_EA87_43df_ABA9_8ED405FC852A/attribute/EAID_2D6A110F_2834_485e_8726_AD8CBDBF5A47>,
